    "updated_at": "2018-08-15T14:55:10Z",
    "body": "Your first phrase is correct.\r\n\r\nThere's no expectation of synchronization between the main thread and the worker thread's rendering/animation. That's a feature of having OffscreenCanvas on a worker: if the main page is blocked/slow/hanging on something, the animation driven by OffscreenCanvas stays as smooth as the browser's rendering can make it.\r\n\r\nThey are supposed to be time-independent and not synchronizable (at least not easily animation synchronizable).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
