    "created_at": "2023-01-26T03:07:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-26T03:07:00Z",
    "body": "Example 1: How does that compare to video? To me, canvas from a worker is similar to video. You don't get much synchronization by default. To sync the main thread with canvas work from a worker AFAIK the solution is supposed to be that you call `transferToImageBitmap` and then `postMessage` that imagebitmap back to the main thread. The main thread then applies that to an `ImageBitmapRenderingContext` exactly when it wants to sync that particular output from the worker with things in the main page. \r\n\r\nExample 2: sounds basically the same. If you want to synchronize, transfer an imagebitmap.\r\n\r\nIt's not clear how `commit` would solve either of these issues. There seems to be an assumption that if `commit` existed it would magically sync. If you call `commit` in the worker and then postMessage back to the main page, and in the main page, use the canvas that was committed it would magically sync but suspect it's not that simple.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
