    "updated_at": "2023-01-26T17:07:22Z",
    "body": "This is the wrong place to address this. Each type of context has it's own needs. If `CanvasRenderingContext2D` has issues here those issues need to be addressed in the `CanvasRenderingContext2D` part of the spec, not the `HTMLCanvasElement` part of the spec.\r\n\r\nAs one solution, you could make it so that all `CanvasRenderingContext2D` commands that affect the contents of the canvas \"if not already queued, queue a task/microtask to update the canvas\". That task would hold references to whatever it needs to make sure the canvas gets updated even if the worker exits, the same way a message send from a worker that closes is still delivered.\r\n\r\n",
