    "updated_at": "2023-01-26T23:26:40Z",
    "body": "I'll have to disagree, here seems like the exact place we need to handle that.  \r\nThis PR changes where the placeholder content gets updated to be on the \"update the rendering\" steps of the OffscreenCanvas context. As currently written, this \"update the rendering\" step can be missed when closing the Worker.  \r\nThis is not a 2D thing, this is what the changes in this PR do, and this concerns any context type since this concerns the placeholder canvas.\r\n\r\nFor the closing Worker case, queuing a task doesn't work, tasks are disregarded. But I guess it could be as simple as adding a clause \"or if the closing flag is set to true\" when determining if this update the rendering step should be ran,  though maybe it needs to be more complex to avoid the animation frame callbacks. But I'm not even sure that would be correct either.",
