    "created_at": "2023-01-27T00:30:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-27T00:30:55Z",
    "body": "It is not the place to handle it. You can not go forcing an API call across contexts. CanvasRenderingContext2D, WebGLRendingingContext, WebGL2RenderingContext, OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D, WebGPURenderingContext, ImageBitmapRenderingContext. They are all disparte APIs. At this level you don't know what implications will be there for the other APIs. For example what if the user calls commit 10 times in a row, 10 times in a row with draw calls between each both of those would make zero sense in WebGPU and all the issues around how to handle it would require a bunch of specification unrelated to any other context. So no, it does not belong here.\r\n\r\nAlso tasks may not run after close but microtasks do\r\n\r\n",
